      "id": 12782,
      "name": "seesome",
      "username": "seesome",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/seesome/{size}/2018_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-04-01T03:26:46.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I noticed something in the digital game and wanted to confirm it here:</p><div><div>\n<p>In the digital game, if I skip my turn due to Meteor Swarm (MS) or the Self-Destruct Sequence (SDS), I can keep cards that would normally require an end of the turn upkeep cost to avoid destruction without paying that cost. I tested this with Gatling Gun, Embolden, and Zealous Offense and if I skipped my turn while those cards were in play, the game skipped over the end of turn phase in which it would have checked to see I wanted to pay the upkeep or let the cards be destroyed.&nbsp; Is this correct?&nbsp; If you skip your turn, you don't have to check end of turn upkeep costs and you get to keep things like the Gatling Gun without discarding a card to pay for it?&nbsp; It seemed odd to me.</p>\n<p>Further, when I tested this with Chastise, which has a start of turn upkeep cost check, I noted one other thing - the game tracked which card came into play first the MS/SDS or Chastise.&nbsp; The card that entered play first was checked first; if it was Chastise, I had to pay to keep it in play, but if it was MS/SDS, I could skip my turn and the game skipped over the rest of my turn, including remainder of the start of turn actions like the upkeep check for Chastise, so I got to keep it in play for free.&nbsp; That was nice, but not how I expected it to play (also difficult as a player as it requires me to keep track of which cards came out first from different decks).</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</div></div><p>&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:44:24.671Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
